-- title:
--   Thickening short exact sequence for an invertible ideal sheaf
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and $\mathcal I$ an ideal sheaf datum on $X$ which is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ has a neighbourhood of the form $X_f$ for some $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$ with $U$ affine open, such that on the affine basic open $X_f$ the ideal $\mathcal I$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor of $\Gamma(X,X_f)$. Let $G$ be an $\mathcal O_X$-module which is invertible, i.e. every point has an open neighbourhood $U$ on which the pullback of $G$ along $U \hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit module, and let $j$ be a natural number. Then there exists a short complex $S$ of $\mathcal O_X$-modules which is short exact, such that: $S.X_1$ is isomorphic to the pushforward along the closed immersion $V(\mathcal I^{j}) \hookrightarrow X$ of the pullback of $G \otimes \mathcal I$ (where $\mathcal I$ denotes the module given by the kernel of the unit map $\mathcal O_X \to$ the pushforward of $\mathcal O_{V(\mathcal I)}$), and there are isomorphisms $e_2$ from $S.X_2$ to the pushforward along $V(\mathcal I^{j+1}) \hookrightarrow X$ of the pullback of $G$ and $e_3$ from $S.X_3$ to the pushforward along $V(\mathcal I) \hookrightarrow X$ of the pullback of $G$, for which the adjunction unit at $G$ for $V(\mathcal I^{j+1}) \hookrightarrow X$, followed by $e_2^{-1}$, then $S.g$, then $e_3$, equals the adjunction unit at $G$ for $V(\mathcal I) \hookrightarrow X$. The isomorphism for $S.X_1$ is asserted only as a nonempty type, and the map $S.f$ is constrained only through the exactness of $S$.
--
--   This is the dévissage sequence $0 \to \mathcal I G/\mathcal I^{j+1}G \to G/\mathcal I^{j+1}G \to G/\mathcal I G \to 0$ attached to an effective Cartier divisor, with the first term identified as the restriction of $G \otimes \mathcal I$ to the $j$-th thickening and the surjection pinned down as compatible with the restriction maps out of $G$. It is used in the study of the relative Picard functor, namely to compute local freeness and determinants of pushforwards along thickenings and to transport the sequence along base change.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_IsInvertible_exists_shortExact_thickening_unit.lean

